**Bug Found and Fixed:**

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element of the array) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). This caused the function to return the wrong word and crash when there was only one word in the input.

**Fix Applied:**
Changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` in src/parse.py:4

All tests now pass successfully!
